{# The one branding partial (D3c, D4b). Renders nothing at all unless a
   `branding` variable was explicitly passed to the template that included
   `base.html.twig` -- inert by default on every page that opts out, which
   is every page except the three tiers named in the architecture's D3.
   No Twig global, no fallback: a missing `branding` variable is silence,
   never a guess.

   `branding is defined` alone is not enough: `TrainerBrandingResolver::forViewerChrome()`
   is a *total* function that legitimately returns `null` for tier A (e.g. a
   coach with no active trainer association right now) -- a defined-but-null
   variable must render nothing too, not crash trying to read a property off
   `null` (a real bug this exact guard shipped with, caught by the S1..S6
   regression suite's `RoleLandingTest` once a coach with no trainer hit a
   branded page). #}
{% if branding is defined and branding is not null %}
    <div class="branding" style="--color-primary: {{ branding.primaryColorHex }}; --color-primary-contrast: {{ branding.contrastColorHex }};">
        {% if branding.hasLogo %}
            <img src="{{ branding.logoUrl }}" alt="Trainer logo" style="max-height: 200px; max-width: 200px; width: auto;">
        {% endif %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
